---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Background and career history of Juho-Pekka Virolainen, SVP of Software Engineering at Sinch and former CTO at IDT Corporation."
  activeNav="about"
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Background</span>
      <h1>Juho-Pekka Virolainen</h1>
      <p>
        Software engineer, former founder, and technology executive based in Finland, focused on
        messaging infrastructure, platform architecture, and practical AI
        systems.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-prose">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          I've spent over thirty years building software products and leading
          engineering organizations across Finland and California. My work sits
          at the intersection of hands-on systems architecture and large-scale
          engineering transformation.
        </p>
        <p>
          For the past quarter-century, most of my focus has been on messaging
          infrastructure, mobile marketing, mobile communications, and
          direct-to-consumer applications. Having seen both the startup and
          corporate sides of the software business, the recurring problem has
          been the same: untangling fragmented systems, aligning architecture
          with how teams actually ship, and turning new technical capabilities
          into reliable commercial infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>Current Role</h2>
        <p>
          Since July 2025, I've served as SVP of Software Engineering at Sinch,
          leading the Messaging engineering organization with a focus on
          platform architecture and engineering transformation.
        </p>

        <h2>Prior Work</h2>
        <p>
          I joined IDT Corporation in 2014 when IDT acquired HDmessaging, where
          IDT had originally been one of our customers. At HDmessaging, we built
          a white-label messaging platform for telecom carriers across the US,
          Europe, and Asia, and created MagicWords, a patented in-chat
          technology (US 20120239761, Linking Context-Based Information to Text
          Messages) that turned words and concepts in live conversations into
          contextual hyperlinks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over more than eleven years at IDT (2014-2025), I served as CTO across
          Messaging, Direct-to-Consumer Products, and the AI Lab. As CTO of
          Messaging (2014-2020), I expanded that stack into IDT's
          next-generation messaging and calling platform used by millions, which
          became the architectural foundation for IDT's broader consumer
          business.
        </p>
        <p>
          As CTO of the Direct-to-Consumer Products group (2020-2024), I led the
          product and engineering transformation across messaging, calling,
          payments, and money transfer. Moving from channel execution to a
          shared platform, unifying separate native mobile apps onto Flutter
          with modular components, and embedding AI into live pricing and
          personalization helped scale the business to millions of users and
          more than $2B in revenue on systems that continue to carry it.
        </p>
        <p>
          In late 2023, I launched and led IDT's AI Lab (2023-2025) to bring
          neural networks and generative AI into production rather than keeping
          them as isolated experiments, building models for pricing, fraud,
          sentiment, UX, and customer support as a structural part of how
          products are designed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before the HDmessaging acquisition, I spent fourteen years co-founding
          and serving as CTO at Silicon Valley mobile startups across messaging,
          mobile marketing, and consumer apps, including Mobicus, Limbo,
          Brightkite, and HDmessaging. Earlier work in the late 1990s included
          rule-based CAD automation (Design++) and real-time website
          personalization.
        </p>
      </div>

